        "role": "user",
        "content": "{\"context\":[],\"filing\":\"MSFT 10-K\",\"section\":\"Part II Item 7\",\"sentences\":[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"section_path\":\"Part II Item 7\",\"text\":\"The following Management’s Discussion and Analysis of Financial Condition and Results of Operations (“MD&A”) is intended to help the reader understand the results of operations and financial condition of Microsoft Corporation.\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"section_path\":\"Part II Item 7\",\"text\":\"MD&A is provided as a supplement to, and should be read in conjunction with, our consolidated financial statements and the accompanying Notes to Financial Statements (Part II, Item 8 of this Form 10-K).\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"section_path\":\"Part II Item 7\",\"text\":\"This section generally discusses the results of our operations for the year ended June 30, 2026 compared to the year ended June 30, 2025.\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"section_path\":\"Part II Item 7\",\"text\":\"For a discussion of the year ended June 30, 2025 compared to the year ended June 30, 2024, please refer to Part II, Item 7, “Management’s Discussion and Analysis of Financial Condition and Results of Operations” in our Annual Report on Form 10-K for the year ended June 30, 2025.\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"section_path\":\"Part II Item 7 > OVERVIEW\",\"text\":\"Microsoft is a technology company committed to making digital technology and artificial intelligence (“AI”) available broadly and doing so responsibly, with a mission to empower every person and every organization on the planet to achieve more.\"},{\"id\":\"s6\",\"section_path\":\"Part II Item 7 > OVERVIEW\",\"text\":\"We create platforms and applications, powered by AI, that deliver innovative solutions that meet the evolving needs of our customers.\"},{\"id\":\"s7\",\"section_path\":\"Part II Item 7 > OVERVIEW\",\"text\":\"We generate revenue by offering a wide range of cloud-based solutions, content, and other services to people and businesses; licensing and supporting an array of software products; delivering relevant online advertising to a global audience; and designing and selling devices.\"},{\"id\":\"s8\",\"section_path\":\"Part II Item 7 > OVERVIEW\",\"text\":\"Our most significant expenses are related to compensating employees; supporting and investing in our cloud-based services, including datacenter operations; designing, manufacturing, marketing, and selling our other products and services; and income taxes.\"},{\"id\":\"s9\",\"section_path\":\"Part II Item 7 > OVERVIEW\",\"text\":\"Highlights from fiscal year 2026 compared with fiscal year 2025 included:\"},{\"id\":\"s10\",\"section_path\":\"Part II Item 7 > OVERVIEW\",\"text\":\"Microsoft Cloud revenue increased 27% to $214.4 billion.\"},{\"id\":\"s11\",\"section_path\":\"Part II Item 7 > OVERVIEW\",\"text\":\"Commercial remaining performance obligation increased 84% to $678 billion.\"},{\"id\":\"s12\",\"section_path\":\"Part II Item 7 > OVERVIEW\",\"text\":\"Microsoft 365 Commercial cloud revenue increased 17%.\"},{\"id\":\"s13\",\"section_path\":\"Part II Item 7 > OVERVIEW\",\"text\":\"Microsoft 365 Consumer cloud revenue increased 28%.\"},{\"id\":\"s14\",\"section_path\":\"Part II Item 7 > OVERVIEW\",\"text\":\"LinkedIn revenue increased 11%.\"},{\"id\":\"s15\",\"section_path\":\"Part II Item 7 > OVERVIEW\",\"text\":\"Dynamics 365 revenue increased 18%.\"}]}"
